{"problem": {"theorem": "Let $f$ be a continuous real function on a metric space $X$. Let $Z(f)$ (the zero set of $f$ ) be the set of all $p \in X$ at which $f(p)=0$. Prove that $Z(f)$ is closed.", "assumptions": [], "domain": "real_analysis", "proof_text": "\begin{proof}

    $Z(f)=f^{-1}(\{0\})$, which is the inverse image of a closed set. Hence $Z(f)$ is closed.

\end{proof}", "explicit_subgoals": []}}

